ktop\": [\n      \"https://coinography.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/coinography-feature-1-1280x698.jpg\",\n      1280,\n      698,\n      true\n    ],\n    \"et-pb-image--responsive--tablet\": [\n      \"https://coinography.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/coinography-feature-1-980x535.jpg\",\n      980,\n      535,\n      true\n    ],\n    \"et-pb-image--responsive--phone\": [\n      \"https://coinography.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/coinography-feature-1-480x262.jpg\",\n      480,\n      262,\n      true\n    ]\n  },\n  \"rttpg_author\": {\n    \"display_name\": \"renu@coinography.com\",\n    \"author_link\": \"https://coinography.com/author/ahmed/\"\n  },\n  \"rttpg_comment\": 0,\n  \"rttpg_category\": \"<a href=\\\"https://coinography.com/category/latest-news/\\\" rel=\\\"category tag\\\">Latest News</a>\",\n  \"rttpg_excerpt\": \"With 10M users, the Dogecoin DeFi DogeOS ecosystem is set to expand beyond CEX trading. Founder Jordan Jefferson details plans for a new on-chain utility economy.\",\n  \"_links\": {\n    \"self\": [\n      {\n        \"href\": \"https://coinography.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts/38187\",\n        \"targetHints\": {\n          \"allow\": [\n            \"GET\",\n            \"POST\",\n            \"PUT\",\n            \"PATCH\",\n            \"DELETE\"\n          ]\n        }\n      }\n    ],\n    \"collection\": [\n      {\n        \"href\": \"https://coinography.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"about\": [\n      {\n        \"href\": \"https://coinography.com/wp-json/wp/v2/types/post\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"author\": [\n      {\n        \"embeddable\": true,\n        \"href\": \"https://coinography.com/wp-json/wp/v2/users/16\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"replies\": [\n      {\n        \"embeddable\": true,\n        \"href\": \"https://coinography.com/wp-json/wp/v2/comments?post=38187\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"version-history\": [\n      {\n        \"count\": 0,\n        \"href\": \"https://coinography.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts/38187/revisions\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"wp:featuredmedia\": [\n      {\n        \"embeddable\": true,\n        \"href\": \"https://coinography.com/wp-json/wp/v2/media/38186\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"wp:attachment\": [\n      {\n        \"href\": \"https://coinography.com/wp-json/wp/v2/media?parent=38187\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"wp:term\": [\n      {\n        \"taxonomy\": \"category\",\n        \"embeddable\": true,\n        \"href\": \"https://coinography.com/wp-json/wp/v2/categories?post=38187\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"taxonomy\": \"post_tag\",\n        \"embeddable\": true,\n        \"href\": \"https://coinography.com/wp-json/wp/v2/tags?post=38187\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"curies\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"wp\",\n        \"href\": \"https://api.w.org/{rel}\",\n        \"templated\": true\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":1003,"aggregated":"{\n  \"id\": 38187,\n  \"date\": \"2026-06-05T02:43:13\",\n  \"date_gmt\": \"2026-06-05T06:43:13\",\n  \"guid\": {\n    \"rendered\": \"https://coinography.com/?p=38187\"\n  },\n  \"modified\": \"2026-06-05T02:43:13\",\n  \"modified_gmt\": \"2026-06-05T06:43:13\",\n  \"slug\": \"dogecoin-defi-dogeos-utility-economy\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"type\": \"post\",\n  \"link\": \"https://coinography.com/?p=38187\",\n  \"title\": {\n    \"rendered\": \"Dogecoin DeFi: DogeOS Founder Says 10 Million Users Can Power a Utility Economy\"\n  },\n  \"content\": {\n    \"rendered\": \"\\n<div class=\\\"wp-block-group\\\"><div class=\\\"wp-block-group__inner-container is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-13d41742 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\\\">\\n\\n<hr />\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The Dogecoin DeFi DogeOS ecosystem is poised for a significant\\ntransformation, according to DogeOS co-founder Jordan Jefferson. In a\\nrecent interview, Jefferson outlined a vision to evolve Dogecoin from a\\ntrading asset into a full-fledged internet economy. He stated that while\\nthe memecoin boasts over 10 million users, its actual on-chain utility\\nis just getting started, with a clear path toward expanding through\\ndecentralized finance and consumer apps.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Most of Dogecoin\\u2019s massive $400 billion to $700 billion annual\\ntrading volume remains locked on centralized exchanges, a structure that\\nJefferson argues fails to benefit the community. This value, he says,\\nneeds to be brought on-chain. <a href=\\\"https://en.bloomingbit.io/feed/news/113592\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\">Source</a></p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\\"wp-block-heading\\\">The Problem:\\nDogecoin\\u2019s Untapped Potential</h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Dogecoin\\u2019s journey is one of cultural phenomenon turned financial\\nasset, but its infrastructure has not kept pace with its popularity.\\nWhile other major blockchains were built by developers and researchers,\\nDogecoin grew organically through internet memes and a powerful\\ncommunity. This unique growth path, however, left a gap in its technical\\nand economic development.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h3 class=\\\"wp-block-heading\\\">An Economy Trapped on\\nExchanges</h3>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The vast majority of Dogecoin activity is speculative trading on\\ncentralized exchanges (CEXs). This creates a scenario where immense\\nvalue is generated, but it rarely flows back into the Dogecoin ecosystem\\nto foster growth or reward holders. \\u201cWe call Dogecoin the people\\u2019s\\ncurrency. But there is still very little people can do with it beyond\\nbuying and selling it on exchanges,\\u201d Jefferson explained. The ecosystem\\nis active in trading, but lacks a functional economy where the currency\\nis used for goods, services, or generating yield.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h3 class=\\\"wp-block-heading\\\">The Burden of Inflation on\\nHolders</h3>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Compounding the issue is Dogecoin\\u2019s inflationary supply model. The\\nnetwork issues approximately 5 billion new coins each year. In\\necosystems like Ethereum or Solana, holders can stake their assets to\\nearn rewards, offsetting this inflation. Dogecoin currently lacks this\\non-chain infrastructure. As a result, the financial impact of the newly\\nminted coins is absorbed entirely by the holders, diminishing their\\npurchasing power over time without a way to put their assets to\\nwork.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\\"wp-block-heading\\\">The Solution:\\nDogeOS\\u2019s Vision for a Utility Economy</h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>DogeOS is focused squarely on building the utility layer that\\nDogecoin has been missing. The project\\u2019s leadership believes the next\\nchapter for Dogecoin is not about speculative price surges, but about\\ncreating tangible use cases. \\u201cDogecoin\\u2019s next phase is about utility,\\nnot price,\\u201d Jefferson stated, emphasizing that users should be able to\\nearn, spend, and interact with their DOGE in a meaningful way.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h3 class=\\\"wp-block-heading\\\">Building On-Chain Income\\nOpportunities</h3>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The primary driver for this shift is the creation of on-chain income\\nopportunities. DogeOS plans to foster an environment for applications\\nacross the DeFi spectrum, including decentralized exchanges (DEXs),\\nlending markets, prediction markets, and stablecoins. The goal is to\\ncreate a vibrant ecosystem of economic activity. Jefferson believes that\\nonce holders have clear opportunities to earn a yield on their Dogecoin,\\nthe migration from CEXs to on-chain wallets will happen naturally. More\\nthan 100 projects are already building within the DogeOS ecosystem to\\nsupport this vision.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\\"wp-block-heading\\\">The\\nAdvantage: Why Community is Dogecoin\\u2019s \\u201cSecret Sauce\\u201d</h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>In a crowded market of blockchain projects, Jefferson is confident\\nthat Dogecoin possesses a unique, inimitable advantage. This advantage\\nis not rooted in superior technology, which he argues can be replicated\\nwith sufficient capital, but in its culture and community.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h3 class=\\\"wp-block-heading\\\">Culture Over Code</h3>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>\\u201cAnyone can build a blockchain with enough money and developers, but\\nyou can\\u2019t create a community,\\u201d Jefferson remarked. Dogecoin\\u2019s global\\nrecognition was not engineered in a boardroom; it grew from years of\\nhumor, authenticity, and internet culture. This cultural power gives it\\na level of brand recognition that new projects struggle to achieve.\\nWhile competing ecosystems are saturated with projects, Dogecoin\\u2019s\\nnative application market remains a relatively open field, offering a\\nmassive opportunity for developers to reach millions of engaged users.\\nThe MyDoge wallet, with over 500,000 users, is already helping to\\nbootstrap this expansion.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\\"wp-block-heading\\\">Conclusion</h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The Dogecoin DeFi DogeOS initiative represents a pivotal moment for\\nthe original memecoin. By focusing on building an on-chain utility\\neconomy, DogeOS aims to convert Dogecoin\\u2019s massive user base from\\npassive holders into active economic participants. This strategy\\naddresses the core issues of exchange dependency and inflation by\\ncreating opportunities for users to earn and transact directly on the\\nblockchain. If successful, it could provide a blueprint for how\\ncommunity-driven assets can mature into robust, decentralized\\neconomies.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\\"wp-block-heading\\\">FAQs</h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>1. What is the main problem DogeOS is trying to solve for\\nDogecoin?</strong></p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>DogeOS aims to solve Dogecoin\\u2019s lack of an on-chain utility economy.\\nCurrently, most activity is trading on centralized exchanges, with\\nlittle value returning to the community, and holders bear the full brunt\\nof the coin\\u2019s inflation without ways to earn yield.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>2. How does DogeOS plan to create a \\u201cutility economy\\u201d for\\nDogecoin?</strong></p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>DogeOS is fostering the development of DeFi applications, including\\ndecentralized exchanges, lending protocols, prediction markets, and\\non-chain games. By creating income opportunities, it encourages users to\\nmove their Dogecoin on-chain and participate in a functional\\neconomy.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>3. Why is Dogecoin\\u2019s reliance on centralized exchanges a\\nproblem?</strong></p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The reliance on centralized exchanges means that the hundreds of\\nbillions of dollars in annual trading volume do not circulate back into\\nthe Dogecoin ecosystem. This prevents the growth of on-chain services\\nand fails to reward the community of holders.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>4. What makes Dogecoin\\u2019s community a unique\\nadvantage?</strong></p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Dogecoin\\u2019s community is a product of years of organic growth through\\ninternet culture, humor, and authenticity. This creates a level of\\nglobal recognition and cultural power that cannot be easily replicated\\nwith capital, giving it a strong foundation for building a new utility\\neconomy.</p>\\n\\n</div></div>\\n\",\n    \"protected\": false\n  },\n  \"excerpt\": {\n    \"rendered\": \"<p>With 10M users, the Dogecoin DeFi DogeOS ecosystem is set to expand beyond CEX trading. Founder Jordan Jefferson details plans for a new on-chain utility economy.</p>\\n\",\n    \"protected\": false\n  },\n  \"author\": 16,\n  \"featured_media\": 38186,\n  \"comment_status\": \"open\",\n  \"ping_status\": \"open\",\n  \"sticky\": false,\n  \"template\": \"\",\n  \"format\": \"standard\",\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"_et_pb_use_builder\": \"\",\n    \"_et_pb_old_content\": \"\",\n    \"_et_gb_content_width\": \"\",\n    \"footnotes\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"categories\": [\n    17\n  ],\n  \"tags\": [],\n  \"class_list\": [\n    \"post-38187\",\n    \"post\",\n    \"type-post\",\n    \"status-draft\",\n    \"format-standard\",\n    \"ha